    {
        "content": "<p>For context, the PR is adding two new <code>lean_lib</code>s <code>Challenge</code> and <code>Solution</code> to the lakefile.</p>",
        "id": 608936334,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1783502147
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have run <code>leanblueprint</code> locally, and then run <code>lake exe checkdecls blueprint/lean_decls</code> (i.e., the command from CI). I don't get such errors. So I cannot even reproduce the error.</p>",
        "id": 608936463,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1783502181
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"238446\">@Anne Baanen</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"556875\">@Pietro Monticone</span> Does one of you have any idea what's going on here?</p>",
        "id": 609457545,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1783690477
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>As a workaround, I certainly don't mind disable the <code>checkdecls</code> step --- would a PR to docgen-action adding such a configuration option be welcome?</p>",
        "id": 609457657,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1783690501
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think this is just because:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>your PR adds <code>Challenge</code> and <code>Solution</code>, but the workflow file in CI <a href=\"https://github.com/fpvandoorn/carleson/blob/b84ab8716935174d37ecc6cfc10251250995c084/.github/workflows/push_pr.yml#L32-L33\">builds only <code>Carleson</code></a></li>\n<li><code>checkdecls</code> <a href=\"https://github.com/PatrickMassot/checkdecls/blob/3d425859e73fcfbef85b9638c2a91708ef4a22d4/Main.lean#L17-L20\">imports every Lean library</a></li>\n</ol>\n<p>so <code>Challenge.olean</code> is missing and that would explain the </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash Session\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"go\">uncaught exception: unknown module prefix 'Challenge'</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is also compatible with the fact that it works locally for you because Comparator <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/comparator/blob/099775bf2e6073fcb22aacd3a2809fdeac3fc84a/Main.lean#L261-L266\">builds both modules first</a>.</p>",
        "id": 609713120,
        "sender_full_name": "Pietro Monticone",
        "timestamp": 1783881736
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok, yes, I have just tested it and building <code>Challenge</code> and <code>Solution</code> in CI seems to fix it.</p>",
        "id": 609713220,
        "sender_full_name": "Pietro Monticone",
        "timestamp": 1783881835
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Very simple, almost embarrassing - thanks a lot for the fix!</p>",
        "id": 609820416,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1783943757
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sure, no problem!</p>",
        "id": 609820530,
        "sender_full_name": "Pietro Monticone",
        "timestamp": 1783943807
    }
]